#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:27
msgid "finalhandler(req, res, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:29
msgid ""
"Returns function to be invoked as the final step for the given `req` and "
"`res`. This function is to be invoked as `fn(err)`. If `err` is falsy, "
"the handler will write out a 404 response to the `res`. If it is truthy, "
"an error response will be written out to the `res` or `res` will be "
"terminated if a response has already started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:35
msgid ""
"When an error is written, the following information is added to the "
"response:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:37
msgid ""
"The `res.statusCode` is set from `err.status` (or `err.statusCode`). If "
"this value is outside the 4xx or 5xx range, it will be set to 500."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:39
msgid "The `res.statusMessage` is set according to the status code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:40
msgid ""
"The body will be the HTML of the status code message if `env` is "
"`'production'`, otherwise will be `err.stack`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:42
msgid "Any headers specified in an `err.headers` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:44
msgid "The final handler will also unpipe anything from `req` when it is invoked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:46
msgid "options.env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:48
msgid ""
"By default, the environment is determined by `NODE_ENV` variable, but it "
"can be overridden by this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:51
msgid "options.onerror"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/finalhandler_README.md:53
msgid ""
"Provide a function to be called with the `err` when it exists. Can be "
"used for writing errors to a central location without excessive function "
"generation. Called as `onerror(err, req, res)`."
msgstr ""

